From: Elian Doran <doran.adoris.elian@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: ov5640: keep the lens when autofocus pauses

Switching autofocus to manual paused the firmware, then moved the lens to
the cached V4L2_CID_FOCUS_ABSOLUTE value, which is not where the firmware
had focused. The controls are also applied again at every stream start,
so any stream restart in manual (e.g. a switch to the full resolution for
a photo) moved the lens away from a tapped focus.

Now manual without a new position keeps the lens where it is and reports
that position (read back from the VCM registers), and the controls
applied at stream start leave the lens alone: its registers keep it while
the sensor is powered.

---
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/ov5640.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/ov5640.c
@@ -3666,6 +3666,23 @@
 					 pos & 0xf));
 }
 
+/* Where the lens is: the code last written, by the firmware or by us */
+static int ov5640_get_focus_position(struct ov5640_dev *sensor)
+{
+	u8 hi, lo;
+	int ret;
+
+	ret = ov5640_read_reg(sensor, OV5640_REG_VCM_CONTROL1, &hi);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+	ret = ov5640_read_reg(sensor, OV5640_REG_VCM_CONTROL0, &lo);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	return FIELD_GET(OV5640_VCM_CONTROL1_CODE_HI, hi) << 4 |
+	       FIELD_GET(OV5640_VCM_CONTROL0_CODE_LO, lo);
+}
+
 /*
  * Point the autofocus at one place in the frame. The zone is a centre on
  * a virtual view finder the firmware sizes itself, so the caller works
@@ -3961,6 +3978,25 @@
 		if (ret)
 			break;
 
+		/*
+		 * Not streaming: the controls being applied again at stream
+		 * start, which would move the lens away from where the
+		 * firmware left it (the registers keep it while powered).
+		 * Manual with no new position: keep the lens where it is and
+		 * report that position, so that pausing does not refocus.
+		 */
+		if (!sensor->streaming)
+			break;
+		if (!sensor->ctrls.focus_absolute->is_new) {
+			ret = ov5640_get_focus_position(sensor);
+			if (ret < 0)
+				break;
+			sensor->ctrls.focus_absolute->val = ret;
+			sensor->ctrls.focus_absolute->cur.val = ret;
+			ret = 0;
+			break;
+		}
+
 		ret = ov5640_set_focus_position(sensor,
 						sensor->ctrls.focus_absolute->val);
 		break;
